ear":2024,"applied":128},{"year":2025,"applied":116}]},"idmc":[],"footnotes":[{"year":null,"population_type":"ASY","text":"The statistics on asylum-seekers (new applications, re-opened/repeat applications and/or appeal application) and refugees individually recognized in Canada include persons who had their claim assessed before the Refugee Protection Division and the Refugee Appeal Division of the Immigration Refugee Board as well as by the Department of Immigration, Refugees and Citizenship Canada through a Pre-Removal Risk Assessment.","view":"asylum"},{"year":null,"population_type":"NAT","text":"Naturalization figures refer to the admission of protected persons as permanent residents of Canada.","view":"asylum"},{"year":2022,"population_type":"REF","text":"A population census in 2021, resulted in a revision of the number of persons under international protection living in Canada, which was previously estimated by UNHCR. Year-end stock refers to protected persons who are yet to acquire permanent resident status.","view":"asylum"},{"year":2022,"population_type":"REF","text":"Refers to people in refugee-like situations.","view":"asylum"},{"year":2023,"population_type":"ASY","text":"The statistics on asylum-seekers (new applications, re-opened/repeat applications and/or appeal application) in Canada include persons who had their claim assessed before the Refugee Protection Division and the Refugee Appeal Division of the Immigration Refugee Board as well as by the Department of Immigration, Refugees and Citizenship Canada through a Pre-Removal Risk Assessment.","view":"asylum"},{"year":2023,"population_type":"REF","text":"Naturalization figures refer to the admission of protected persons as permanent residents of Canada. End-year stock refers to protected persons who are yet to acquire permanent resident status. The statistics on refugees individually recognized in Canada include persons who had their claim assessed before the Refugee Protection Division and the Refugee Appeal Division of the Immigration Refugee Board as well as by the Department of Immigration, Refugees and Citizenship Canada through a Pre-Removal Risk Assessment.","view":"asylum"},{"year":2024,"population_type":"REF","text":"End-year stock refers to protected persons who are yet to acquire permanent resident status.","view":"asylum"},{"year":2025,"population_type":"REF","text":"Naturalization figures refer to the admission of protected persons as permanent residents of Canada. End-year stock refers to protected persons who are yet to acquire permanent resident status. The statistics on asylum-seekers (new applications, re-opened/repeat applications and/or appeal application) and refugees individually recognized in Canada include persons who had their claim assessed before the Refugee Protection Division and the Refugee Appeal Division of the Immigration Refugee Board as well as by the Department of Immigration, Refugees and Citizenship Canada through a Pre-Removal Risk Assessment. Updated figures for the number of Ukrainians within the Canada-Ukraine authorization for emergency travel (CUAET) program have been reflected in the reported figure for people in a refugee-like situation.","view":"asylum"}],"sources":["unhcr_countries","unhcr_population","unhcr_demographics","unhcr_idmc","unhcr_solutions","unhcr_asylum_applications","unhcr_footnotes","wpp_population","natural_earth"]}
